8 questions x 3 runs, 4 attempts each

  error style     right    wrong  gave up  ran out  mean calls
  terse            3/24     0/24    18/24     3/24         2.4
  instructive     21/24     0/24     3/24     0/24         2.8

  wrong = a valid call with the wrong metric or region, which the tool accepted

When the model gave up after terse errors, it said, for example:
  "I couldn’t retrieve that because the metric name I used wasn’t valid for the warehouse tool. If you want, I can try again with a different m…"

When the model gave up after instructive errors, it said, for example:
  "I couldn’t retrieve “turnover” because the warehouse tool doesn’t recognize that metric. Available metrics are: - revenue - gross_profit - m…"

What each error says:
  terse        Error: invalid metric.
  instructive  Error: unknown metric 'sales'. Valid metrics are: revenue (sales value), gross_profit, margin_pct (gross margin as a percentage), orders, units (items sold). Retry with one of these exactly.
  terse        Error: invalid region.
  instructive  Error: unknown region 'midwest'. Did you mean 'Midwest'? Retry with a valid region exactly.
